  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indonesia Digital Health and Workforce Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is arranged under Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with National Health Services England (NHS England) to provide flexible, strategic and technical health expertise to the Government of Indonesia for digital health and workforce planning. The subject matter experts are derived from NHSC Member organisations, through the NHS Consortium Technical Advisory Service (CTAS). 

The project covers from period of 1 April 2023 to 31 March 2025, but this AMP will only cover remaining activities starting from August 2024 to March 2025. 

The workforce mainstream is mainly related on workforce planning and stroke care workforce collaboration. The stroke care workforce has entered its Year 2 of implementation, focusing on stroke care service design, workforce, training and education in Indonesia. Year 2 activities will include Communities of Practice for different categories of stroke care professions and policymakers, Actions Learning Sets, and adaptation of Fundamentals of Acute Care and Treatment after Stroke (FACTS) e-module. The main stakeholders are the Ministry of Health and Rumah Sakit Pusat Otak Nasional.</narrative>
  </description>
